.TH "HTMLTEXTAREAELEMENT.SELECT_EVENT" "3JS" "October 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLTextAreaElement.select_event \- HTMLTextAreaElement: select event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]select\f[B]\f[R] event of the
\f[CR]HTMLTextAreaElement\f[R] interface fires when the selection\(cqs
extent or direction is changed programmatically, or when the user
selects text.
.PP
For general information about this event, see
\f[CR]HTMLInputElement\f[R]: \f[CR]select\f[R] event.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqselect\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onselect = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A generic \f[CR]Event\f[R].
